# everyone trusts someone; whoever is trusted is vouched for; so someone is
# vouched for.  Trying cases cannot decide it (some within all, over a
# relation); a proof does
atom	trusts(x,y)	x trusts y
atom	vouched(x)	x is vouched for
domain	alice
P1	S1	all x: some y: trusts(x,y)
P2	S2	all x: all y: trusts(x,y) -> vouched(y)
C	S3	some y: vouched(y)
